WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:03.420
Claude Code. Copilot. Cursor.

00:04.140 --> 00:06.790
Every AI agent wants its own rules file.

00:07.290 --> 00:10.410
Copy them by hand, and they quietly drift apart.

00:11.800 --> 00:13.380
PromptScript fixes that.

00:13.910 --> 00:17.520
Write your AI rules once, and every agent follows them.

00:18.600 --> 00:21.700
Start from your company base, add shared fragments,

00:21.960 --> 00:26.150
then describe who the agent is, your standards, and your hard limits.

00:26.610 --> 00:28.630
All in one small source file.

00:29.600 --> 00:31.940
Run prs compile.

00:32.550 --> 00:35.970
PromptScript writes native files for fifty AI coding tools.

00:36.610 --> 00:41.820
CLAUDE.md, Copilot instructions, Cursor rules, AGENTS.md.

00:42.470 --> 00:44.670
Each in the format its tool expects.

00:45.700 --> 00:47.580
Rules inherit like code.

00:48.180 --> 00:54.140
Your organization sets the base, teams extend it,
and projects override only what they need.

00:54.810 --> 00:58.130
Change a policy once, and it reaches every repo.

00:59.100 --> 01:03.260
Before anything ships, strict validation catches prompt injection,

01:03.560 --> 01:07.400
encoded payloads, invisible Unicode, and suspicious links.

01:07.960 --> 01:10.330
Bad rules never reach your agents.

01:11.300 --> 01:14.570
Install skills like packages, from any Git repo.

01:15.110 --> 01:19.010
They are pinned in a lockfile, and land natively in every agent.

01:20.500 --> 01:23.380
For your own apps, release prompts like code.

01:23.970 --> 01:29.590
Content-hashed bundles move from staging to prod,
with sign-off for one exact version.

01:30.600 --> 01:34.580
PromptScript. One source of truth for every AI agent.

01:35.080 --> 01:38.230
Open source, at getpromptscript.dev.
